.IX Title "RRDPYTHON 1"
.TH RRDPYTHON 1 2026-08-08 1.11.0 rrdtool
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
rrdpython \- About the RRD Python bindings
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\& import rrdtool
\& rrdtool.create(\*(Aq/tmp/test.rrd\*(Aq, \*(AqDS:foo:GAUGE:20:0:U\*(Aq)
.Ve
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBrrdtool\fR functions are directly callable via the Python programming
language. This wrapper implementation has been written from the scratch
(without  SWIG)
.PP
The API expects strings and/or a list of strings as parameters to the functions.
Please refer to the other \fBrrdtool\fR documentation for functions and valid arguments.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
.SS "Example 1"
.IX Subsection "Example 1"
.Vb 3
\& import sys
\& sys.path.append(\*(Aq/path/to/rrdtool/lib/python2.6/site\-packages/\*(Aq)
\& import rrdtool, tempfile
\&
\& DAY = 86400
\& YEAR = 365 * DAY
\& fd,path = tempfile.mkstemp(\*(Aq.png\*(Aq)
\&
\& rrdtool.graph(path,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-imgformat\*(Aq, \*(AqPNG\*(Aq,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-width\*(Aq, \*(Aq540\*(Aq,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-height\*(Aq, \*(Aq100\*(Aq,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-start\*(Aq, "\-%i" % YEAR,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-end\*(Aq, "\-1",
\&              \*(Aq\-\-vertical\-label\*(Aq, \*(AqDownloads/Day\*(Aq,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-title\*(Aq, \*(AqAnnual downloads\*(Aq,
\&              \*(Aq\-\-lower\-limit\*(Aq, \*(Aq0\*(Aq,
\&              \*(AqDEF:downloads=downloads.rrd:downloads:AVERAGE\*(Aq,
\&              \*(AqAREA:downloads#990033:Downloads\*(Aq)
\&
\& info = rrdtool.info(\*(Aqdownloads.rrd\*(Aq)
\& print info[\*(Aqlast_update\*(Aq]
\& print info[\*(Aqds[downloads].minimal_heartbeat\*(Aq]
.Ve
.SS "Example 2"
.IX Subsection "Example 2"
.Vb 3
\& import sys
\& sys.path.append(\*(Aq/path/to/rrdtool/lib/python2.6/site\-packages/\*(Aq)
\& import rrdtool
\&
\& # in real life data_sources would be populated in loop or something similar
\& data_sources=[ \*(AqDS:speed1:COUNTER:600:U:U\*(Aq,
\&                \*(AqDS:speed2:COUNTER:600:U:U\*(Aq,
\&                \*(AqDS:speed3:COUNTER:600:U:U\*(Aq ]
\&
\& rrdtool.create( \*(Aqspeed.rrd\*(Aq,
\&                 \*(Aq\-\-start\*(Aq, \*(Aq920804400\*(Aq,
\&                 data_sources,
\&                 \*(AqRRA:AVERAGE:0.5:1:24\*(Aq,
\&                 \*(AqRRA:AVERAGE:0.5:6:10\*(Aq )
.Ve
.PP
If you use the \fBsite\-python\-install\fR make target you can drop to first sys.path.append
line since the RRDtool module will be available everywhere.
.PP
If RRDtool runs into trouble, it will throw an exception which you might want to catch.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
rrdcreate, rrdupdate, rrdgraph, rrddump, rrdfetch, rrdtune, rrdlast,
rrdxport, rrdinfo
